{"id": "EUVD-2026-76252", "enisaUuid": "8c8b075d-167e-38e2-ace8-aed1f42de722", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsysctl: move the \"cad_pid\" entry from pid_table[] to kern_reboot_table[]\n\ncad_pid is global, and kill_cad_pid() is only used in the root namespace.\n\nHowever, due to pid_table_root_permissions(), a non-root user can unshare\npid/user namespaces and modify it from the child namespace. This makes no\nsense and is simply wrong.\n\nMove it to kern_reboot_table[] where it logically belongs; this ensures\nthat only GLOBAL_ROOT_UID can read/modify this sysctl.\n\nNote that this patch doesn't preserve \"#ifdef CONFIG_PROC_SYSCTL\" around\nthe \"cad_pid\"; CONFIG_PROC_SYSCTL selects CONFIG_SYSCTL, so it is always\nset when kern_reboot_table[] is compiled.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:13", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8527de7fea191fda704792a56081f9009aeec37", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a09bc4eaa67e1a72df3b6d0beb3afeef1e1fdfcd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7170ca01623b399c97f2ae9d3e228badc1f25ea3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80929", "GHSA-5367-6mxw-83v4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "155412e6-e23d-3e48-b95d-bc84dd42443c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e054bcbe7e7af2baad3752f1a4916a7fffc0457e <7170ca01623b399c97f2ae9d3e228badc1f25ea3"}, {"id": "3365afca-3831-3517-ac7c-57c33c153210", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "38ab069b-a481-3eab-a306-13c680a74c55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "6539c215-d765-3f0a-82f9-af30ba17efc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "745af9fc-a7d4-3662-aefe-8830e8559d45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7f3b24de-f3dc-303d-9dc0-5197ef9fe208", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e054bcbe7e7af2baad3752f1a4916a7fffc0457e <a09bc4eaa67e1a72df3b6d0beb3afeef1e1fdfcd"}, {"id": "7f63a63a-c83c-330f-a91a-25508f779b4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e054bcbe7e7af2baad3752f1a4916a7fffc0457e <e8527de7fea191fda704792a56081f9009aeec37"}, {"id": "fbaf740b-9a10-39bc-87e9-cc28475d58c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "878e8e58-3dca-31b1-90c9-e622dafce560", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}